SUMMARY:The Great Allentown Fair
DESCRIPTION:Established in 1852\, The Great Allentown Fair is one of the oldest and largest annual agricultural festivals in the United States. Held every late August through Labor Day at the 46-acre Allentown Fairgrounds\, this Lehigh Valley tradition seamlessly blends its rural heritage with modern entertainment. \nVisitors can explore livestock exhibits and Agri~Land barnyard tours\, or witness high-stakes culinary contests in the Agri~Plex. The iconic Grandstand hosts world-class concerts and the fan-favorite demolition derby\, while the bustling midway offers thrilling rides and classic fair food like funnel cakes and Ritz Barbecue. It remains a premier destination for family-friendly education and “Home Grown Fun”. \n\nSee our schedule of Fairs & Festivals in Lancaster County and surrounding areas.\nOther Things To Do in Lancaster\, PA\n\n\nArt Galleries\nDistilleries\nEscape Rooms\nFactory Tours\n\n\n\nIndoor Things To Do\nMassage and Spas\nOutdoor Things To Do\n\n\n\nShooting Ranges\nTheaters\nWineries\nAll Things To Do in Lancaster
URL:https://lancasterpa.com/events-calendar/allentown-fair/
